---
description: AI, ATS, matching, and cover-letter generation rules
globs: lib/openai/**,app/api/**/analyze*/**,app/api/**/generate*/**,app/api/profile/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# AI rules

- All AI provider calls must run server-side.
- Never expose API keys in client code.
- The CV and job description are source data.
- Do not invent candidate experience, skills, results, education, or company facts.
- Store prompt versions when generated content is persisted.
- AI failure must not corrupt job or application records.
- Batch operations must return individual success and failure results.

# Domain expectations

- ATS analysis: surface detected keywords, missing keywords, and actionable CV suggestions without fabricating credentials.
- Matching score: explain fit from CV + job text; do not silently overwrite user data on failure.
- Cover letters: personalize from CV + job only; preserve existing generate / save / copy flows.
- CV parsing: prefer structured extraction into the existing profile schema; keep local fallback behavior when present.
